Typeface
────────
  Any family name from fonts.google.com, spelled as it is on the family's page.

  DM Sans            geometric, large x-height, reads well from 11sp to 32sp
  Inter              the safe choice; designed for screens, very neutral
  Plus Jakarta Sans  a little more character, good for consumer apps
  Manrope            rounder and friendlier, slightly less good at small sizes
  Figtree            warm and open; strong at display sizes

Font [DM Sans]: Monospace font [JetBrains Mono]: 
Look and feel
─────────────
  The brand colours. Every shade of each, pressed, subtle and the dark-theme
  versions, is derived from these, with the launcher icon's background and
  whether text on each is black or white.

Primary hex [#2C6BED]: 
  Leave either blank and it is worked out from the primary: the same hue with
  the chroma taken out for the secondary, a sixth of a turn round the wheel for
  the tertiary.

Secondary hex: Tertiary hex: 
  How controls respond to a finger.

  1. Standard
     Crisp, a trace of overshoot. Lively without asking for attention.
  2. Bouncy
     Springy, with a visible overshoot. Playful; wrong for anything
     financial.
  3. Calm
     No overshoot anywhere, slightly longer. For dense, professional
     interfaces.
  4. Snappy
     The shortest response that still reads as motion. For utilities.

  Which [1]: 
  What the components look like: corners, borders, fields and the tab bar together.

  1. Utility
     Cool neutrals, hairline outlines, a floating tab bar. Tools, finance,
     admin.
  2. Social
     Brand-tinted surfaces, pill buttons, heavier headlines, a floating tab
     bar. Feeds and chat.
  3. Editorial
     Warm paper and ink, large tight display type, underlined fields.
     Reading and news.
  4. Playful
     Cream surfaces, extra-bold type, thick outlines and offset shadows.
     Games and kids.

  Which [1]: 
  Haptics are a light vibration when a control responds. The device's own setting
  always applies on top.
  Haptics on by default? [Y/n]: 
